# Testing

## Layout

| Folder | Runner | What |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `tests/data/` | Vitest (`*.test.ts`) | Checks on the dataset |
| `tests/search/` | Vitest (`*.test.ts`) | Parsing, matching, the typo rule, scoring, concept tagging |
| `tests/queries/` | Vitest (`*.test.ts`) | The PRD's test queries (section 7), end to end through the search core |
| `tests/e2e/` | Playwright (`*.spec.ts`) | One scenario per Must story, on the built app |

## Rules

- **Red first.** A new test must fail for the right reason before the code is written.
- **Never weaken, skip or delete a test to make it pass.** If a test seems wrong, say so and explain why.
- `tests/queries/` mirrors PRD section 7 exactly. A new query goes in the PRD table and in the test, together.
- Test behaviour, not implementation: assert on what `search()` returns, not on internal helpers, unless the helper is a documented rule (e.g. the 30% typo rule).
- Include the traps from data discovery: "sleep" must never return Insomnia, Vital Spirit or Rest; "drain" and "trainer" must never return rain results.
- In end-to-end tests, find elements by role and accessible name (`getByRole`), not by CSS class.
- Failure messages should say which item failed (e.g. `expect(x, pokemon.name)`).
